Error [E0702]: `s` can't use `mut` at the FFI boundary
  --> tests/ui/ffi_bad_type.jet:2:16
    |
  2 |     fn bad(mut s: String) -> String = "std::convert::identity";
    |                ^
 Why: foreign functions take owned copies — `mut`, `take`, and `view` aren't allowed here
 Fix: remove the access keyword and pass by value

Error [E0102]: nothing named `bad` exists here
  --> tests/ui/ffi_bad_type.jet:6:11
    |
  6 |     print(bad("hi"))
    |           ^^^
 Why: only functions that have been defined (or built in, like `print`) can be called
 Fix: define it first (fn bad() { ... }), or call one that exists
